SUMMARY:University of Toronto Antenna Measurement Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a full-day\, in-person workshop on antenna measurements\, bringing together students\, young professionals\, researchers\, and industry professionals for a combination of expert lectures and live demonstrations. \nThe workshop will feature Prof. Yahya Rahmat-Samii\, Distinguished Professor at UCLA\, and Dr. Vincent Rodriguez\, Staff Electromagnetic Engineer at NSI-MI Technologies and Chair of the IEEE AP-S Technical Committee on Antenna Measurements. Sessions will cover antenna theory fundamentals\, practical measurement considerations\, and key antenna measurement standards. \nParticipants will also have the opportunity to attend live near-field and far-field antenna measurement demonstrations in anechoic chambers at the University of Toronto\, providing a practical look at measurement setups\, procedures\, and techniques. \nThe event is jointly hosted by the IEEE AP-S Technical Committee on Antenna Measurements\, IEEE AP-S Standards Committee\, IEEE AP-S University of Toronto Student Branch Chapter\, and IEEE Toronto Section. \nRegistration is free and open to students and young professionals.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/university-of-toronto-antenna-measurement-workshop/
LOCATION:Bahen Centre for Information Technology\, 40 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 2E4\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
