SUMMARY:Emerging Leaders Workshop - Leadership 101
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, October 28 | 10:00 AM – 3:00 PM | Register in Advance \nThe Emerging Leaders Workshop is Leadership 101 for FASE students. This interactive one-day program equips aspiring leaders with the foundational skills\, confidence\, and mindset needed to take on leadership roles in student clubs\, campus initiatives\, and beyond. Designed for students with little or no formal leadership training\, it serves as the perfect starting point for your leadership journey.  \nDate: Wednesday\, Oct 28   \nTime: 10:00 am-3:00 pm  \nLocation: St. George campus (exact location to be confirmed upon acceptance).   \n*Lunch and snacks will be provided.   \n\nWorkshop spaces are limited and all applicants will be contacted to confirm their acceptance. \n\n\nIt is expected that accepted participants prioritize program attendance\, except in case of extenuating circumstances (e.g. illness) in which case staff should be informed in advance. \n\nProgram Registration closes on Thursday\, October 22nd\, 2026 at 11:59pm  \nQuestions? Vivian Trumblay\, Leadership Education Specialist vivian.trumblay@utoronto.ca  \nEmerging Leaders 2026 Workshop Application – Fill out form 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/emerging-leaders-workshop-leadership-101/
LOCATION:St. George campus (exact location to be confirmed upon acceptance)
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
