SUMMARY:Crash Course for Building & Leading Teams
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, October 29 | 10:00 AM – 3:00 PM | Register in Advance \nDesigned for current FASE club leaders\, this interactive workshop will strengthen your team building and management skills through a leadership-focused lens. Participants will explore strategies for creating inclusive team environments\, fostering engagement\, and leading teams effectively toward shared goals. While the workshop is structured as a two-part series\, participants are welcome to attend either session individually or join both for the full experience.  \nDate: Thursday\, October 29  \nTime: 10:00 AM – 3:00 PM  \nLocation: St. George campus (exact location to be confirmed upon acceptance).   \n*Lunch and snacks will be provided.   \nPart I (10:00am-12:00pm): Building Inclusive Teams  \nPart II (1:00pm-3:00pm): Leading Effective Teams  \n\nWorkshop spaces are limited and all applicants will be contacted to confirm their acceptance.  \n\n\nIt is expected that accepted participants prioritize program attendance\, except in case of extenuating circumstances (e.g. illness) in which case staff should be informed in advance.  \n\nProgram Registration closes on Sunday\, October 25th\, 2026 at 11:59pm  \nQuestions? Vivian Trumblay\, Leadership Education Specialist vivian.trumblay@utoronto.ca   \nISTEP Crash Course for Building & Leading Teams – Fill out form 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/crash-course-for-building-leading-teams/
LOCATION:St. George campus (exact location to be confirmed upon acceptance)
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
