UID:10004772-1794398400-1794402000@www.engineering.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Lunch & Learn — Game on: Leveling up pediatric rehab with gaming technologies
DESCRIPTION:Register now!\n					\n				\n	What if rehabilitation felt more like playing your favorite video game?   \nAdvances in gaming technology\, artificial intelligence and interactive design are transforming how children and youth participate in therapy and rehabilitation. In this talk\, Professor Elaine Biddiss will share how researchers\, clinicians\, families and young people are collaborating to create engaging technologies that make rehabilitation more accessible\, motivating and effective. Through real-world examples\, she will explore how game-based interventions are helping children develop skills\, build confidence and participate more fully in everyday life.  \nJoin us on November 11\, 2026\, at our monthly Skule™ Lunch & Learn.  \n	By registering for the Skule™ Lunch & Learn event\, you could potentially earn Continuing Professional Development (CPD) credits. CPDs are essential for professional engineers and limited license holders to renew their licenses annually through the PEO PEAK Program. If you’re wondering whether this event offering qualifies you for CPD credits\, click here to learn more. \n	About the speaker \n				\n	Dr. Elaine Biddiss \n	Professor Elaine Biddiss is an associate professor at the Institute of Biomedical Engineering\, a senior scientist at Holland Bloorview Kids Rehabilitation Hospital and a member of the Rehabilitation Sciences Institute.   \nWorking with families\, clinicians and an interdisciplinary team\, Dr. Biddiss designs innovative technologies that create possibilities for young people with disabilities to participate more enjoyably and effectively in arts\, music\, physical activities and therapies. Her research activities include the engineering aspects of system design (machine learning\, computer vision\, biomechanics\, wearable sensors and user-centred design) as well as clinical evaluation (single case experimental design\, outcome assessment\, technology-assisted and remote assessment\, home-based therapy). Dr. Biddiss is passionate about expanding access to healthcare\, education and leisure opportunities through low-cost\, accessible technologies. 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/lunch-learn-game-on-leveling-up-pediatric-rehab-with-gaming-technologies/
LOCATION:Online
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
